The first momentum projection is not yet acceptable: it returns \(3.3215\pm0.2344\), outside the pre-registered window, despite 96% channel weight. The culprit is identifiable—the reference bound packet is shifted by the same scattering event, so projecting onto its unshifted free packet feeds hard-leg recoil into the soft phase. I’m switching that projection to a fixed-\(K\) two-string eigenwave; its propagation phase is momentum-independent and cancels from the derivative.
